hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1408","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of His father, he said: So-and-so sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying for rain. He said: “The Messenger of God went out May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, submissive, supplicating, and humble. He did not deliver a sermon like yours, and he prayed two rak’ahs.”"
